Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:48:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1190/1265] ggml: sync to upstream 0.26.0

The vendored fork rebases onto ggml-org/ggml 0.26.0, which now carries
the fixes upstreamed from these projects:

- Vulkan: mul_mat and mul_mat_id read strided views such as a KV cache
  slice with their real batch stride, and mul_mm keeps exact A and B
  ranges (ggml-org/llama.cpp#28956)
- Metal: GGML_OP_PAD supports left and circular padding
  (ggml-org/llama.cpp#29561)
- CUDA: bitonic argsort handles rows wider than 1024 without CUB, on
  HIP and MUSA (ggml-org/llama.cpp#28957)

Two commits remain on top of upstream:

- cpu: fused snake activation
- ggml: conv_1d result layout for batched input
  (ggml-org/llama.cpp#28738)

(cherry picked from commit 05ca71c115f0410b39d0332037691cecf98f5ded)
